From cd51742048c45e715cd704f940608ac2649c04e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:29:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/15] Accept reviewed text and boolean catalog values in
 manifests

Manifests could only carry numbers, so a disclosed non-numeric field such
as dividend_payment_frequency had no ingestion path. A typed_facts
section now publishes through the existing typed publisher after checking
the field is a data_points catalog field of the declared text or boolean
type, the value and period are valid, and a page and table are cited;
numbers are refused there. Market valuations read decimal rows only, as
the other numeric readers already do.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CfTpoii6QDStyTPdotmEdY
---
